WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.089
Like all comic book universes, DC Comics is
made up of a sprawling canon of fan-favorites

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.620
and total busts.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.980
On one hand, you've got your holy trinity
of Superman, Batman, and Wonder Woman.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.960
On the other hand, you've got the likes of
Pandora, Azrael, or Jason Todd as Robin.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.220
Everyone has their favorites, their worsts
and firsts but what about lifelong comics

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.880
fan and comic actor Jason Mewes?

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.460
We had the opportunity to speak with Mewes
aka Jay, of Jay and Silent Bob fame while

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.460
he was promoting his film Madness in the Method,
which he stars in and directed as his debut

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.820
feature behind the camera.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.940
Knowing that he knows his stuff when it comes
to comic books, we asked him for his take

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.060
on the three best and three worst characters
DC Comics has to offer.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.960
"If we're going powerhouses, I have my favorites,
but again I wouldn't say they're the strongest.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:58.800
But I would have to say for a team I would
say Batman, Superman, and Martian Manhunter.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.780
Because Martian Manhunter, to me, has just
as much power and such as Superman.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.519
He does have weaknesses.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.180
But he can turn intangible and invisible and
such.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.640
Mewes was clear that with his selection of
favorites, he mostly went for raw strength

00:01:13.649 --> 00:01:17.710
over scrappy personality, and that he might
personally prefer some characters who don't

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.700
hit quite so hard.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.380
"I love Deadshot too as a character.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.170
Deadshot's one of my favorite characters.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:25.040
And yeah, and Vigilante, but they're not very,
you know…"

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:29.880
After selecting his top three, Mewes had a
surprising amount of trouble getting into

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.020
the DC Comics characters he likes least.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.260
In general, the real-life Jay doesn't seem
to dislike much of anything.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:41.060
When it comes to fandom, he's like a living
embodiment of that one song from The LEGO

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:41.560
Movie.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.140
"I would say worse characters...

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.460
I mean I don't think there is worse characters.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.780
I mean again it’s… they're all sort of
awesome."

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.020
But then, in a eureka moment, he started seeing
double, and found two of his worsts in one

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:58.520
shot.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.440
"The freaking Wonder Twins.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.820
I mean I know they can turn into most things,
but in the cartoon, they only turn into like

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.240
water and ice and hawks and stuff.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:12.880
I'm sure they could turn maybe into like dragons
and maybe something cooler, but maybe not.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.980
So those two are the worst off the top of
my head."

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.160
"You were terrific, Zan.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.280
First a wave, now a drip."

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.440
So that's two.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.180
Sorry, Zan and Jayna, but when it comes to
superhero tier lists, apparently you're down

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.640
there with the likes of King Tut.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:38.040
"Another worst, I would say, I don't know
why, I'm not a fan of if we're going old school,

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.120
King Tut, or like I'm not a fan of the Penguin.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.360
I know he was sort of cool, but not really."

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:49.200
In selecting his three worst DC characters,
Mewes spent a lot of time expounding on the

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.680
comic book brand's villains, which he says
include some of his favorite comic book characters

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.320
in general.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:59.200
Of particular note for him outside of his
top three is the whole collection of Batman's

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:04.079
rogues' gallery, including Two-Face, The Riddler,
and all the other fiends and foes who tend

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.380
to cross paths with justice in Gotham City.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:11.220
It's not just what they do in comics, cartoons,
and on film that makes them neat to him.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:15.020
It's also all the toy sets they end up in,
which he has a habit of collecting.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:19.420
"I would say, I mean the Rogues from DC and
Batman.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:26.230
I mean I love all the sets they have of, again
going from me from collecting toys, like the

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:31.700
Rogues Gallery and stuff, like Clay Face,
and Joker, Poison Ivy, all that stuff are

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:32.580
pretty awesome.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.940
And then I love Suicide Squad from the comics.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:43.900
You know, so Harley Quinn is pretty cool,
and Joker, and Deadshot's on that team.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.940
Not the Fresh Prince of Bel-Air's Deadshot."

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.600
"Y'all jokers must be crazy."

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:59.980
Outside of his top and bottom three, it's
clear Mewes knows a thing or two about DC

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.820
Comics characters, probably as much, if not
more, than the actors who actually play them

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.360
in adapted form on screen.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:11.540
He's an actor, so it begs the question would
he ever want to suit up to play a DC Comics

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.099
hero or villain himself?

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:16.669
"And I would say no, because I love.

00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:21.030
Like I'm not saying I would turn them down
But I don't think I'd want to play a character

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:27.870
because I love watching the movies, the TV
shows so much."

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:33.110
On top of checking out Jason Mewes' directorial
debut Madness in the Method, out now via video

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:38.210
on demand, you can also see him in the upcoming
View Askewniverse sequel Jay and Silent Bob

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.720
Reboot, touring the United States in a roadshow
format starting October 15.

